# Notification Deadline

This scope computes a notification deadline relative to a
trigger date. It handles both "no later than X before event"
and "no later than X after event" patterns.

Source pattern: carryover and transfer notifications in EU
trade agreements.
Example: "Kazakhstan shall notify the Community no later than
31 March of the following year if it intends to make use of
this provision."
Example: "Kazakhstan shall notify the Community no later than
31 May if it intends to make use of this provision."

```catala
declaration scope NotificationDeadline:
  input trigger_date content date
  input notification_window content duration
  input deadline_is_before_trigger content boolean
  output notification_deadline content date
```

## Deadline before trigger

When the deadline falls before the trigger date (e.g. "no
later than X days before end of year").

```catala
scope NotificationDeadline:
  date round down
  definition notification_deadline under condition
    deadline_is_before_trigger
  consequence equals
    trigger_date - notification_window
```

## Deadline after trigger

When the deadline falls after the trigger date (e.g. "within
X days of the request").

```catala
scope NotificationDeadline:
  definition notification_deadline under condition
    not deadline_is_before_trigger
  consequence equals
    trigger_date + notification_window
```
